{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "MadronichCloudGrid",
    "description": "The cloud-refined radiative-transfer grid of WRF-Chem's Madronich photolysis, on a FIXED grid padded with zero-thickness layers (chem/module_phot_mad.F:2205-2320, WRF v4.8.0).\n\nTHE PROBLEM THIS SOLVES. subgrid inserts extra levels inside cloud, so `nlevel` is a function of the cloud field -- 70, 72, 77 and 78 at the four dumped daytime calls of the reference run. An esm index set has a size fixed at load, so a grid whose SIZE is state-dependent cannot be one. Everything upstream in this chain was therefore written for a clear column.\n\nWHY THE PADDING IS NOT AN APPROXIMATION -- and precisely what it is, because an earlier draft of this description overstated it. The argument was: a padded level duplicates the top level, so its layer has dz = 0 and hence taun = 0; in ps2str a zero-optical-depth layer gives expon = exp(0) = 1, so cup = cuptn and cdn = cdntn, the layer's two continuity rows reduce to identities, and the solution is unchanged. That is correct for taun = 0, but TWO facts break it as an exact identity. (1) WRF floors dtscat and dtabs at 1/largest = 1e-36 each (module_phot_mad.F optics), so a padded layer carries tau = 2e-36, omega = 0.5, g = 0 -- not tau = 0. (2) SUBROUTINE sphers divides by each layer's thickness to form the slant ratio dsdh, which is 0/0 on a zero-thickness layer. WRF never meets that case, so the guard that resolves it (dsdh := 0; see MadronichOpticalDepth.dsdh) is NEW LOGIC WITH NO FORTRAN COUNTERPART. An audit of every division in the chain whose denominator involves a height or thickness found dsdh to be the ONLY one that can reach zero on the padded grid; the others all act on the 70-level input grid, which the padding never touches.\nWhat is TRUE, and measured on all four dumped columns (nlevel 70, 72, 77, 78) in float64: the padded solve equals the unpadded one to at most 1.8e-13 on fluxes of order one, at every real level. The value the guard assigns does not matter -- dsdh := 0 and dsdh := its true finite secant limit agree to 3e-15 -- because a padded layer's dsdh is multiplied by taun = 2e-36. The 1.8e-13 that remains is float64 rounding from a 262-row elimination instead of a 150-row one, nine orders of magnitude below the precision to which WRF's own single-precision solve determines these fluxes (1.8e-4 clear, 5.8e-4 cloudy). So: equal to WRF's unpadded computation to float64 roundoff. Not an approximation in any sense that reaches a test, but not bit-identical either, and it rests on a guard that is new logic.\n\nNO RECURRENCE IS NEEDED HERE. The emission counts are pointwise; the running level index the Fortran carries is a prefix COUNT of them, which telescopes to a contraction; and the inverse map from an RT level back to the model level that emitted it is another contraction (how many model levels start at or below it) rather than a search. Only the two-stream solve downstream needs a causal self-reference.\n\nBOUNDS, AND WHAT HAPPENS OUTSIDE THEM -- THE RUN STOPS. This component reproduces subgrid for ONE inserted level per cloudy half-layer (idt = 1) on a grid of NRT levels, and it refuses to run outside that rather than return a grid that is silently wrong. Two conditions are checked.\n(1) idt > 1. subgrid inserts idt = max(ifix(cloud*dzt*0.02), 1) levels into each cloudy half-layer, so a half-layer optical depth of 50 or more needs more than one. The emission rule here assumes one, and without the check it would simply UNDER-COUNT: for a single very thick cloud layer WRF emits 77 levels and the unchecked rule emits 72, with no overflow and no error. That is the more dangerous of the two failures, since deep convection reaches it well inside NRT. The reference SCM never does -- its largest half-layer optical depth is about 11.\n(2) nlevel > NRT. With idt = 1 and cloud confined to the 60 model levels, which MadronichColumnSetup guarantees, 70 <= nlevel <= 130, and NRT = 131 leaves one spare. It can be exceeded only if a consumer supplies cloud above the model top (139 for all 70 input levels) or once idt > 1 is supported.\nHOW THE RUN IS STOPPED. Each condition gathers a shaped PARAMETER sentinel -- `idt_supported` (one entry) at max_idt, `rt_level_capacity` (NRT entries) at the raw level count -- and multiplies the result into nlevel, so the gather cannot be skipped. In range it reads 1.0 and changes nothing. Out of range it raises `E_TREEWALK_CONSTARRAY_OOB`, which is fail-closed by CONFORMANCE_SPEC section 5.5.5 ('the zero-ghost convention is never applied to a const-array gather'); the Rust engine latches that fault and raises it after evaluation rather than returning a number. The messages are, verbatim: `const array 'idt_supported' index 4 out of range 1..1` and `const array 'rt_level_capacity' index 139 out of range 1..131` -- the index is what the cloud field needs, the range is what this component supports. Verified by tools/check_cloud_grid_bounds.py, which drives the current file past each bound and asserts both messages, and asserts that an in-range column still passes. An esm inline test cannot express an expected failure, which is why that check is a script.\nTwo cautions. The sentinels must stay PARAMETERS: an observed takes the zero-ghost convention instead and returns 0 silently -- measured -- which would turn the check back into the silent failure it replaces. And they must never be given a `periodic` or `clamp` boundary policy, which would do the same. This is deliberately NOT built on a closed-function error such as interp_non_monotonic_axis: in the Rust binding every closed-function error is replaced by NaN on the evaluation path (EarthSciAST #443), whereas the const-array gather fault is not. Only the Rust binding has been run against these checks, although section 5.5.5 is normative for all of them.\n\nREPRODUCED, NOT CORRECTED: the air density on inserted levels goes through WRF's log-linear interpolation, which divides by a SUM of heights where a difference belongs (FORTRAN_BUGS B11). It therefore does NOT return `air(i)` at `z = zz(i)`: on the reference column the air at inserted-grid levels that coincide exactly with model levels is wrong by 4.9 percent at model level 55 rising to 8.9 percent at level 60. It feeds every pressure-quenched quantum yield. Since the purpose of this component is to reproduce WRF, the bug is transcribed as written and flagged here; `j_hcocho` is the channel it moves most.\n\nINTERPOLATION. Where subgrid calls trapez to carry ozone and aerosol onto the layer mid-points, this uses lib/table_interp.esm over the 70-level input interfaces (the bracket zmid_bracket once, then interp_linear_bracketed for each field): interp.linear's semantics, bit for bit (count the interfaces at or below the mid-point to bracket it, gather the two bracketing nodes, one linear blend), written out because the table and axis here are run-time columns and esm-spec section 9.2 admits only literal const arrays in the closed function. It CLAMPS outside the axis where trapez writes a 1e-12 sentinel -- a difference that cannot trigger here, since every mid-point lies inside the input grid. It could NOT be used on the padded RT axis itself: like interp.linear it assumes a strictly increasing axis, and the padding repeats values. trapez's other use -- carrying the j-values from the RT grid back onto the model levels -- needs no interpolation at all, because every model interface is itself a node of the RT grid; the consumer reads the coinciding node directly.\n\nPORTABILITY: until 2026-10-16 this component passed `ze`, `o3_node` and `aer_node` to interp.linear as VARIABLE references, which esm-spec section 9.2's load-time error table forbids (`interp_table_not_const` / `interp_axis_not_const`) and which the Rust native compiler refuses. The const rule stands (decided 2026-10-16, the question EarthSciAST #443 raised), so the interpolation is now written with lib/table_interp.esm and no closed function sees a run-time table."
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NN": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 70,
      "description": "Interfaces of the extended input column: 60 WRF w-levels plus 10 above-model levels."
    },
    "NRT": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 131,
      "description": "Size of the padded radiative-transfer grid. 131 is the maximum this 60-model-level configuration can need with one inserted level per emission; see the description for what happens if a consumer exceeds it."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "node": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NN"
    },
    "rt": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NRT"
    },
    "rt_lay": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
          "NRT",
          1
        ]
      }
    },
    "idt_cap": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 1
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "MadronichCloudGrid": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../../../lib/table_interp.esm"
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "par": {
          "ref": "./madronich_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "ze": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "km",
          "description": "Interface heights of the extended column (MadronichColumnSetup.ze), 60 model w-levels plus 10 above-model levels.",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ],
          "default": 0.0
        },
        "t_node": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Temperature on those interfaces.",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ],
          "default": 250.0
        },
        "air_node": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "cm^-3",
          "description": "Air number density on those interfaces.",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ],
          "default": 1e+19
        },
        "cloud_node": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/km",
          "description": "Cloud extinction on those interfaces.",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ],
          "default": 0.0
        },
        "is_cloudy": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 where the interface carries cloud.",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ]
        },
        "prev_clear": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when the interface below is clear (or this is the bottom); this is what triggers the cloud-base midpoint emission.",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ]
        },
        "n_emit": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "How many radiative-transfer levels this model level emits: 1 if clear, 2 at the bottom, otherwise prev_clear + 1 + (1 unless at the top).",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ]
        },
        "start": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Number of RT levels emitted below this model level -- a prefix COUNT, written as a contraction, not a recurrence.",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ]
        },
        "start1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1-based index of this model level's first emitted RT level.",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ]
        },
        "nlevel": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Number of ACTIVE radiative-transfer levels, WRF's nlevel: nlevel_raw once both bound checks have passed, and identical to it whenever they do. For a cloud field confined to the 60 model levels, which MadronichColumnSetup guarantees, 70 <= nlevel <= 130; NRT = 131 leaves one spare. See the description for what happens outside that."
        },
        "L_eff": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "RT level index clamped to nlevel: every padded level above nlevel evaluates as a DUPLICATE of the top active level, which is what makes the padding zero-thickness.",
          "shape": [
            "rt"
          ]
        },
        "src": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Which model level emitted this RT level, found by counting how many model levels start at or below it.",
          "shape": [
            "rt"
          ]
        },
        "slot": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Position of this RT level within its model level's emissions, 0-based.",
          "shape": [
            "rt"
          ]
        },
        "kind": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "What this RT level IS: 0 at the model interface itself, 1 the cloud-base midpoint below it, 2 the midpoint above it.",
          "shape": [
            "rt"
          ]
        },
        "z_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "km",
          "description": "Radiative-transfer interface heights, padded. This is subgrid's `z`.",
          "shape": [
            "rt"
          ]
        },
        "zt_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Temperature on the RT grid, subgrid's `zt`.",
          "shape": [
            "rt"
          ]
        },
        "zair_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm^-3",
          "description": "Air number density on the RT grid, subgrid's `zair`. NOTE: at a cloudy level this is NOT air_node even where z_rt equals ze exactly -- WRF's interpolation divides by a SUM of heights where a difference belongs, so it is off by up to 8.9 percent. That is FORTRAN_BUGS B11, and it is reproduced here rather than corrected because the point of this component is to match WRF.",
          "shape": [
            "rt"
          ]
        },
        "vcld_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/km",
          "description": "Cloud extinction carried by each RT level, subgrid's `vcld` before it is multiplied by the layer thickness.",
          "shape": [
            "rt"
          ]
        },
        "dz_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "km",
          "description": "Layer thickness on the padded grid. EXACTLY ZERO for every padded layer, which is what makes the padding a no-op.",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ]
        },
        "vt_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Layer-mean temperature, subgrid's vt.",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ]
        },
        "vair_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm^-2",
          "description": "Layer air column, subgrid's vair. Zero on padded layers.",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ]
        },
        "vcld_lay": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Layer cloud optical depth, subgrid's vcld after it is multiplied by dz. Zero on padded layers.",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ]
        },
        "o3_node": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ],
          "units": "cm^-3",
          "default": 1000000000000.0,
          "description": "Ozone number density on the input interfaces, AFTER the 325 DU rescaling (MadronichColumnSetup.o3_node)."
        },
        "aer_node": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ],
          "units": "1/km",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Aerosol extinction on the input interfaces."
        },
        "zmid_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "km",
          "description": "Layer mid-points of the padded grid; zero-thickness layers collapse onto the top level.",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ]
        },
        "zmid_bracket": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ],
          "description": "Lower bracketing index of each RT layer mid-point on the input interfaces ze (the number of interfaces at or below it, held to [1, NN-1]; lib/table_interp.esm bracket_index); shared by the ozone and aerosol lookups."
        },
        "o3_mid": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm^-3",
          "description": "Ozone interpolated onto the layer mid-points: this is `trapez` as subgrid calls it, written as interp_linear_bracketed on the bracket zmid_bracket (lib/table_interp.esm: interp.linear's semantics for a run-time table) over the 70-level INPUT interfaces. That axis is strictly increasing, which the bracket requires. It CLAMPS outside the axis where trapez writes a 1e-12 sentinel -- a difference that never triggers here, because every layer mid-point lies inside [ze(1), ze(NN)].",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ]
        },
        "aer_mid": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/km",
          "description": "Aerosol extinction interpolated onto the layer mid-points, likewise interp_linear_bracketed on zmid_bracket.",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ]
        },
        "vo3_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm^-2",
          "description": "Layer ozone column. Zero on padded layers.",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ]
        },
        "vaer_raw_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Layer aerosol optical depth before normalization.",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ]
        },
        "vaer_total": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Column total, the normalization denominator."
        },
        "vaer_rt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Layer aerosol optical depth normalized to unit column, subgrid's vaer.",
          "shape": [
            "rt_lay"
          ]
        },
        "nlevel_raw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Number of radiative-transfer levels subgrid emits for this cloud field, before the two bound checks. Read `nlevel` instead: it is this value once both checks have passed."
        },
        "idt_below": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "How many levels subgrid would insert in the half-layer BELOW this cloudy interface, max(ifix(cloud*dzt*0.02),1) with dzt the half-layer thickness. 1 wherever this component's emission rule applies."
        },
        "idt_above": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "node"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The same for the half-layer ABOVE."
        },
        "max_idt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Largest idt anywhere in the column. This component implements idt = 1 ONLY; see the description. Exposed so the regime is visible and assertable, and fed into the idt check that stops the run when it is exceeded."
        },
        "idt_check": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1.0 when max_idt = 1; otherwise the gather raises and the run stops."
        },
        "rt_check": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1.0 when nlevel_raw <= NRT; otherwise the gather raises and the run stops."
        },
        "idt_supported": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [
            "idt_cap"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "BOUND SENTINEL, not data -- do not override it. A one-entry array gathered at max_idt: in range when max_idt = 1, and otherwise the gather raises `E_TREEWALK_CONSTARRAY_OOB: const array 'idt_supported' index <max_idt> out of range 1..1`, which reads as 'subgrid needed idt = <max_idt>, this component supports 1'. It must be a PARAMETER: an observed would take the zero-ghost convention and return 0 silently."
        },
        "rt_level_capacity": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [
            "rt"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "BOUND SENTINEL, not data -- do not override it. An NRT-entry array gathered at nlevel_raw: in range when the grid fits, and otherwise the gather raises `E_TREEWALK_CONSTARRAY_OOB: const array 'rt_level_capacity' index <needed> out of range 1..<NRT>`, which names both the level count the cloud field needs and NRT. Its length follows NRT automatically, which a literal array would not. It must be a PARAMETER: an observed would take the zero-ghost convention and return 0 silently."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "is_cloudy",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "node"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": ">",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "cloud_node",
                        "i"
                      ]
                    },
                    0
                  ]
                },
                1,
                0
              ]
            },
            "args": [
              "cloud_node"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "prev_clear",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "node"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "<=",
                  "args": [
                    "i",
                    1
                  ]
                },
                1,
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    1,
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "is_cloudy",
                        {
                          "op": "min",
                          "args": [
                            "NN",
                            {
                              "op": "max",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    1
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "args": [
              "is_cloudy"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "n_emit",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "node"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "==",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "is_cloudy",
                        "i"
                      ]
                    },
                    0
                  ]
                },
                1,
                {
                  "op": "ifelse",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "<=",
                      "args": [
                        "i",
                        1
                      ]
                    },
                    2,
                    {
                      "op": "+",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "prev_clear",
                            "i"
                          ]
                        },
                        1,
                        {
                          "op": "ifelse",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "<",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                "NN"
                              ]
                            },
                            1,
                            0
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "args": [
              "is_cloudy",
              "prev_clear"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "start",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "node"
              },
              "j": {
                "from": "node"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "<",
                  "args": [
                    "j",
                    "i"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "n_emit",
                    "j"
                  ]
                },
                0
              ]
            },
            "args": [
              "n_emit"
            ],
            "reduce": "+"
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "start1",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              "start",
              1
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "nlevel_raw",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "start1",
                  "NN"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "n_emit",
                      "NN"
                    ]
                  },
                  1
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "L_eff",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "L"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "L": {
                "from": "rt"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "min",
              "args": [
                "L",
                "nlevel"
              ]
            },
            "args": []
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "src",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "L"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "L": {
                "from": "rt"
              },
              "i": {
                "from": "node"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "<=",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "start1",
                        "i"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "L_eff",
                        "L"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                1,
                0
              ]
            },
            "args": [
              "L_eff",
              "start1"
            ],
            "reduce": "+"
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "slot",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "L"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "L": {
                "from": "rt"
              }
